From d86b845df160d39ca990c950041d557a96a3554d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gurdal Oruklu <gurdaloruklu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 11:17:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Support per-PID dump directory and compression via v2 service
 protocol

Rework of RDK-47153 patch to apply on top of lazy-pages changes.
The zstd compression backend was already present in compress.c;
this commit adds the service protocol extensions for per-PID options.

Changes:
- memcrclient_proto.h: Add MEMCR_CMDS_V2 command, checkpoint options
  enum (MEMCR_CHECKPOINT_DUMPDIR, MEMCR_CHECKPOINT_COMPRESS_ALG),
  memcr_compress_alg enum, and struct service_options
- memcr.c: Replace single dump_dir with allowed_dump_dirs list
  (semicolon-separated via -d), add set_dump_dirs(),
  is_dump_dir_path_allowed(), read_command_v2() for v2 protocol
  parsing, set_checkpoint_options_dfl() for per-PID option dispatch
  in forked workers, SERVICE_MODE_SOCKET_TIMEOUT_MS, update
  service_command() to accept checkpoint_options, update all
  cleanup_pid() call sites for new dump_dir parameter
- memcr-client.c: Add -d (dump dir), -z (compress algorithm), -v
  (force v1 protocol) options. Default to v2 protocol with
  send_cmd_v2() that sends MEMCR_CMDS_V2 envelope followed by
  the actual command and options payload
- README.md: Document per-PID dump directory, v2 protocol client
  usage

The v2 protocol is backward-compatible: old clients sending v1
commands (100/101) are handled normally. The v2 envelope uses
MEMCR_CMDS_V2 (102) as the outer command with payload length in
the pid field, followed by the real command and optional TLV
checkpoint options.
